        "The README describes request-triggered bounded memory caching: 30 seconds fresh, at most five minutes old while revalidating. Private access/permission checks remain separate. [R6]",
        "These are this adapter's policies, not a guarantee for every JSON service or of new business data every five minutes."
      ]
    ],
    "sourceNote": "Radar feeds do not reuse web cookies, store feed credentials or follow redirects; the README currently directs authenticated feeds to file export. This differs from configuring a browser workbench origin. Do not fix access by exposing public ports, removing authentication or putting passwords in URLs; use the existing authorized private path. [R2][R5]",
    "stateTitle": "Read-only → explicit phone confirmation → receipt or uncertain-stop",
    "stateIntro": "This is the optional write path described by source/README, not permission enabled by this fixture: reply_supported=false and no reachable service are provided. Actual replies require separate server authorization and eligible original items.",
    "flow": "Read snapshot / filter (no status write)\n    ↓\nEligible original target + separate server write authorization?\n    ├─ No → read-only / retain draft → stop\n    └─ Yes → fetch fresh target/version → full phone review + explicit confirmation\n                 ↓\n           persist the same request_id → server submission\n                 ├─ recorded receipt → recorded, awaiting owner handling (not execution/acceptance)\n                 └─ timeout / uncertainty → freeze input, read back the same request; no blind resend\nChanged target/source → fresh read and confirmation; unresolved is not proof of no write",
